  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nSaturday-Wednesday:\nLingering showers and a few thunderstorms taper off to the south\nand east on Saturday, with a ridge quickly rebuilding to our\nwest. This will support increasing mid-level heights across the\narea, with highs varying from upper 80s (east) to middle 90s\n(west). This will be accompanied by increasing dewpoints and\nhumidity.\n\nEnsemble guidance is coming into better agreement that the next\npotential heat wave really takes shape on Sunday into early\nnext week. This can be gleaned from a shrinking interquartile\nspread, with highs progged to range from middle to upper 90s,\nwith 100s across southeast KS into far southwest MO. The eastern\nportion of our area look to remain on the eastern periphery of\nthe ridge through early next week, which will keep them slightly\n\"cooler\". Nonetheless, these temperatures are 5 to 10 degrees \nabove normal for our area in late July. Meanwhile, heat index \nvalues appear to be in the 100 to 110 degree range, though some\nlingering uncertainty still exists on how well we mix each day \nin addition to existing variance in dewpoints ranging from 60s \nto 70s. As we progress through the end of the week into the \nweekend, we will need to address the potential for heat \nheadlines going forward into early next week. Rain chances \nremain minimal (< 10%) during this timeframe.",
